input:
Evaluate \begin{align*}
\left(c^c-c(c-1)^c\right)^c
\end{align*} when $c=3$.

solution_steps:
First, substitute $c=3$ into the expression:
\begin{align*}
\left(3^3-3(3-1)^3\right)^3
\end{align*}
Simplify the expression inside the parentheses:
\begin{align*}
\left(3^3-3(2)^3\right)^3
\end{align*}
Calculate the exponents:
\begin{align*}
\left(27-3(8)\right)^3
\end{align*}
Perform the multiplication and subtraction inside the parentheses:
\begin{align*}
(27-24)^3
\end{align*}
Calculate the exponent:
\begin{align*}
3^3
\end{align*}
Perform the exponentiation:
\begin{align*}
27
\end{align*}
So, the value of the expression is $\boxed{27}$.The answer is: 27

