solution_steps:
We can rewrite the expression as
\begin{align*} \left| \frac{\beta - \alpha}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \right| &= \left| \frac{\beta - \alpha}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \cdot \frac{\overline{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta}}{\overline{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta}} \right| \\ &= \left| \frac{\overline{\beta} - \overline{\alpha}}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \right| \\ &= \left| \frac{\overline{\beta - \alpha}}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \right| \\ &= \left| \frac{\overline{\beta - \alpha}}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \cdot \frac{1}{\overline{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta}} \right| \\ &= \left| \frac{\overline{\beta - \alpha}}{\overline{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta}} \right| \\ &= \left| \frac{\overline{\beta} - \overline{\alpha}}{\overline{1} - \overline{\overline{\alpha} \beta}} \right| \\ &= \left| \frac{\overline{\beta} - \overline{\alpha}}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \overline{\beta}} \right| \\ &= \left| \frac{\overline{\beta} - \overline{\alpha}}{1 - \overline{\alpha \beta}} \right|. \end{align*}
Since the conjugates of complex numbers have the same magnitude, this expression is equal to $\boxed{1}$.The answer is: 1

