We can simplify each of the factors modulo 20:
\begin{align*}
77 &\equiv -3 \pmod{20}, \\
88 &\equiv 8 \pmod{20}, \\
99 &\equiv -1 \pmod{20}.
\end{align*}
Then we can compute the product modulo 20:
\begin{align*}
77\cdot 88\cdot 99 &\equiv (-3)(8)(-1) \pmod{20} \\
&\equiv 24 \pmod{20} \\
&\equiv \boxed{4} \pmod{20}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: 4

